  description: Four-chambered muscular organ powering systemic and pulmonary circulation.
  arterialSupply: Left & Right Coronary Arteries (arising from aortic sinuses).
  innervation: Cardiac plexus (Vagus nerve [CN X] parasympathetic & T1-T4 sympathetic).
  clinicalFunction: Pumps ~70 mL/beat, maintaining ~5 L/min cardiac output.
  commonPathology: Coronary artery disease, myocardial infarction, arrhythmias.
